WEBVTT

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:27.270
Tarou.

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:27.560
Tarou?

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:30.270
Tarou!

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:31.690
Hey, Tarou!

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:37.570
Tarou, I've been calling you. Is something wrong with your ears?

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:37.570
<i>Shut up.</i>

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:42.120
Booze. Go buy me some more.

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:44.750
No way.

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:48.620
Why are you drinking so early in the afternoon?

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:50.380
Don't you feel bad about wasting the day?

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:50.380
<i>The hell?</i>

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:51.790
You little bastard!

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:59.260
Why should I have to look after my father?

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:00.220
Screw you.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:01.180
Yo, everyone,

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:03.510
let's hurry up and get away from this shitty house.

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:03.510
<i>Okay.</i>

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:05.310
Let's go.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:11.900
Tango, Tango. The stray cat, Tango. Tango.

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:12.320
Tang—

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:13.320
Hey, Kinoko!

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:14.820
What happened to cleaning the drains?

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:17.950
Tonkichi, aren't you going to finish your lunch?

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:19.160
Hey, Hyoromatsu,

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:20.320
where are you going?

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:22.910
Sachi, you have to babysit!

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:23.950
What's going on?

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:25.790
Don't leave me out.

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:27.960
We're supposed to be a team!

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:30.630
<i>I thought they would behave better once Joe left.</i>

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:41.930
Damn it!

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:43.850
Isn't there anything fun to do?

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:45.970
Damn it.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:49.980
Damn it.

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:52.560
Everything we do is boring.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:54.480
Hey, kids.

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:55.650
Huh?

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:58.400
Can I ask for directions?

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:01.450
Why?

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:03.160
Are you new or something?

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:06.700
Sorry, but I was wondering where Namida Bridge is.

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:08.870
I don't know this area.

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:10.290
Namida Bridge? Wait a second.

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:11.790
Hey, Tarou.

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:15.290
Namida Bridge! This might be...

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:18.510
It's from Joe!

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:19.880
I thought so.

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.890
Really? Let me see!{Mumbling, mostly incoherent}

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:20.970
<i>Yay!</i>

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:26.720
Joe is human after all.

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:30.350
He's locked in a cell on an isolated island, so he probably misses his home town.

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:35.230
He remembers me like a second father. Let's see.

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:36.820
Hey, old man, what did he write?

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:37.940
Hurry up and read it!

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:39.650
Hurry up, old man!

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:43.860
This is... This is the same postcard I sent to him.

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:45.910
Huh?

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:49.330
It's returned to the sender by his request.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:52.960
Joe,

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:55.460
why don't you read my letters?

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:59.090
Your replies are all that I have to keep me going, Joe.

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:36.540
Well, his life's not in danger, right?

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:38.630
Yes, he should be okay.

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:42.920
He only suffered a concussion, but he's still stunned.

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:46.550
His outburst only hurt his pride.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:49.890
You should let him rest. He's not ready to be moved yet.

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:07.030
That idiot. He looks so stupid, lying in that bed like an invalid.

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:08.160
It's not even funny.

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:11.490
New guys can't break out that easily.

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:15.370
Just look at me, I've been here for three years!

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:18.330
It's easy to get in, but hard to get out!

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:24.050
Joe, the guy who beat you, Rikiishi, is famous for his strength.

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:27.260
There's no way you could have won. It was impossible.

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:35.480
Joe, I'll just keep writing.

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:37.020
It doesn't matter how many times.

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:38.270
I won't stop...

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:46.280
...until my letters convince you to take boxing seriously.

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:50.320
Old man, you're not giving up yet?

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:54.830
Oh, you guys again?

00:05:55.910 --> 00:05:58.830
We wrote a letter for Joe, too.

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:00.250
What did you write?

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:01.840
It's a secret. Right, guys?

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:04.510
Secret, secret!

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:06.510
I hope Joe reads it.

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:08.050
In it goes.

00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:09.340
Okay.

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:11.350
Enter.

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:17.480
Rikiishi?

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:18.770
Are you here to visit Yabuki?

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:24.230
He's still out cold.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:31.240
He's waking up!

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:35.330
Yabuki! Hey, Yabuki!

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:58.180
You're finally awake, Yabuki. You failed to escape.

00:06:58.180 --> 00:07:02.060
We can thank Rikiishi's powerful punch for that.

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:06.610
Ri-kiishi.

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:07.650
Ri-kiishi.

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:08.150
That's right.

00:07:08.150 --> 00:07:10.990
Rikiishi Toru, a welterweight pro boxer.

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:12.280
The Six-Round Boy.

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:27.880
After his debut, he won thirteen fights in a row.

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:32.180
His strength simply overwhelmed everyone he faced,

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:34.680
he was far too strong and aggressive.

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:46.270
But even he had a weak point...

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:48.440
<i>You suck!</i>

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:51.070
<i>The fight was fixed!</i>

00:07:56.620 --> 00:08:03.210
After one match, he punched an obnoxious spectator and almost killed him.

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:12.130
After that, he was called a heartless killer and was banned from boxing.

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:18.100
He couldn't just sit around and not fight anymore.

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:42.620
Upset by the decision, 
he became extremely violent.

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:47.040
He ended up making this place his home, with you.

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:49.630
That about sums it up.

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:04.850
This is Yabuki Joe?

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:07.440
You disappoint me.

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:09.480
<i>...with a drilling motion, punch!</i>

00:09:08.770 --> 00:09:12.070
When you hit me with that sudden left jab,

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:13.110
<i>Punch, punch, punch!</i>

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:14.400
it actually made me feel happy.

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:16.240
It looked professional.

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:19.450
I thought you were a real pro,

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:22.450
but you went down too quickly.

00:09:22.450 --> 00:09:25.750
Everything after that punch was pathetic.

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:24.960
<i>Bastard, I'm going to kill you!</i>

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:34.260
You're such an amateur.

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:44.430
Hey, hey, Rikiishi, gloating over a victory like this isn't like you.

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:54.570
Rikiishi, what are you doing!?

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:55.150
Stop it!

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:17.670
Rikiishi, stop this!

00:10:17.670 --> 00:10:18.470
Won't you stop!?

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:29.810
Don't worry. I was just checking to see if you were telling the truth.

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:32.480
Wh-What were you checking for?

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:37.490
Well, I was making sure he really was the loser.

00:10:39.860 --> 00:10:41.450
Sorry to interrupt.

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:56.510
He didn't react to Rikiishi being right in front of him?

00:10:56.510 --> 00:11:00.010
Yes, he should have regained consciousness.

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:06.010
So you mean Rikiishi's punch hurt Yabuki's pride more than his body?

00:11:06.010 --> 00:11:07.890
His spirit is broken.

00:11:07.890 --> 00:11:12.020
Unless something changes, he might not
recover even if he regains consciousness.

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:14.610
That's okay, isn't it?

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:17.030
It would be good for everyone if he could grow up a little.

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:21.110
Really. If another person escaped, it would come out of our salaries.

00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:30.040
Warden's office.

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:32.040
It looks like Yabuki has escaped!

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:32.880
Wh-What!?

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:33.500
Wh-What!?

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:40.010
H-He got out! R-Ring the alarm!

00:11:49.470 --> 00:11:52.020
What's going on? What's happened?

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:10.700
I did it! I escaped!

00:12:23.510 --> 00:12:25.430
Hey!

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:27.720
Hey, Rikiishi!

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:31.520
Rikiishi, you have to help us.

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:34.480
I'll shorten your sentence if you catch him.

00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:35.810
Mr. Guard,

00:12:35.810 --> 00:12:37.440
don't be so hasty.

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:40.730
I'm willing to bet that he'll come back.

00:12:41.610 --> 00:12:43.490
I'm sure of it.

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:45.490
Wh-What do you mean?

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:51.370
He can't just run away and forget about me.

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:55.500
Even though he was knocked down, he didn't look defeated.

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:59.090
He won't lose even if it kills him.

00:13:09.470 --> 00:13:10.850
Serves you right!

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:15.060
Escaping was a piece of cake!

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:19.980
I wish I could see the stupid look on their faces!

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:54.310
<i>Bastard!</i>

00:14:05.650 --> 00:14:07.070
Damn it!

00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:10.820
Damn...

00:14:22.790 --> 00:14:28.930
<i>Loser... Loser... Loser!</i>

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:40.810
Damn it. I'll swim.

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:54.830
Shit.

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:03.920
Joe!

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:04.840
Joe.

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:07.090
Your sparkling eyes yell "Tomorrow."

00:15:07.090 --> 00:15:08.670
You are my tomorrow.

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:09.670
You are Tomorrow's Joe!

00:15:09.670 --> 00:15:12.720
Get out of here.

00:15:09.670 --> 00:15:12.720
<i>Get out of here.</i>

00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:15.140
<i>Joe, get out of here.</i>

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:18.350
<i>I'll do what I can from here!</i>

00:16:14.360 --> 00:16:17.370
Hey, young man, what are you doing in a place like this?

00:16:18.030 --> 00:16:19.870
You're not killing yourself, are you?

00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:24.880
Taking a sun bath? That's nice.

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:30.380
"That's nice"? Are you senile, old man?

00:16:31.210 --> 00:16:33.340
Probably, I'm old.

00:16:34.970 --> 00:16:41.390
It's a tough job bringing all these letters to the prison. Say, could you deliver them for me?

00:16:42.430 --> 00:16:43.640
These letters?

00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:48.110
That's a good joke.

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:50.360
You want me to deliver letters to the prison I just escaped from?

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:54.910
H-Hey stop that!

00:16:58.370 --> 00:17:01.830
That's a good one! What a great joke!

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:13.840
Tarou?

00:17:15.260 --> 00:17:16.430
And Kinoko too?

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:18.680
Here's one from Hyoromatsu.

00:17:18.680 --> 00:17:19.350
Sachi too.

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:21.850
What a surprise.

00:17:22.850 --> 00:17:25.850
When did they learn how to write?

00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:30.730
Dear Joe, are you well?

00:17:30.730 --> 00:17:31.900
We're okay.

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:34.530
We really miss you because you're gone.

00:17:34.530 --> 00:17:37.490
Old man Danpei is having a hard time because you're not responding,

00:17:37.490 --> 00:17:39.070
so please write to him.

00:17:39.070 --> 00:17:42.080
Old Danpei is always saying, "for the sake of tomorrow."

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:43.870
He just keeps on saying that.

00:17:43.870 --> 00:17:49.380
"He dreams of you training to become a boxer. So do I."

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:53.210
I don't know how to write very well, so I drew you a picture instead.

00:17:53.210 --> 00:17:55.920
This is you being a champion.

00:17:55.920 --> 00:17:57.380
Isn't it cool?

00:17:58.180 --> 00:18:00.850
Is this me? What a bad drawing.

00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:05.390
You're Yabuki Joe? This one is for you too.

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:18.200
<i>You disappoint me.</i>

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:22.200
<i>That first punch was great, but 
everything after it was pathetic.</i>

00:18:24.660 --> 00:18:28.750
<i>That's right, Joe, aim for the center. Use a drilling motion.</i>

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:31.210
<i>All right, come at me!</i>

00:18:43.890 --> 00:18:45.390
I see.

00:18:45.390 --> 00:18:49.690
Only the left jab I learned from Danpei was a real punch.

00:18:49.690 --> 00:18:50.690
Interesting.

00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:56.690
I'll do whatever you say, old man.

00:18:56.690 --> 00:18:59.150
There's no other way.

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:14.420
Rikiishi-san, sorry, but I'll escape later.

00:19:14.420 --> 00:19:16.050
I don't care if you're a pro boxer,

00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:18.470
or if you think my punch is pathetic.

00:19:19.380 --> 00:19:25.510
I won't be happy until I land some more punches on that crooked nose of yours.

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:29.680
Just you wait, Rikiishi. I haven't lost yet!

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:33.690
I haven't lost!

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:36.500
Rikiishi, I'm coming back to fight you one more time.

00:20:44.720 --> 00:20:46.140
Danpei!

00:20:45.050 --> 00:20:46.140
<i>Old man!</i>

00:20:47.260 --> 00:20:49.310
Come on out!

00:20:51.470 --> 00:20:52.480
Old man!

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:56.560
Why are you making such a racket so early in the morning?

00:20:57.520 --> 00:20:58.610
It came!

00:20:59.070 --> 00:21:01.780
Look, a postcard from Joe!

00:21:01.780 --> 00:21:05.740
What? He returned it again?

00:21:06.110 --> 00:21:07.700
Not at all.

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:08.320
Look!

00:21:08.320 --> 00:21:11.120
Come on, it's a letter from Joe.

00:21:11.120 --> 00:21:12.950
Wh-What!?

00:21:17.080 --> 00:21:18.790
I'll skip the greeting.

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:23.760
Send as many boxing tips as you can. No holding back.

00:21:23.760 --> 00:21:28.680
There's someone here I really need to beat.

00:21:28.680 --> 00:21:35.640
"He is a strong and worthy opponent.

00:21:35.640 --> 00:21:38.810
I also learned that right straight.

00:21:38.810 --> 00:21:43.690
Because of a couple of issues with an escape,

00:21:43.690 --> 00:21:47.160
I'll be in solitary confinement for a while.

00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:51.950
So I have a lot of time to train.

00:21:51.950 --> 00:21:54.330
Take care of things for me.

00:21:54.330 --> 00:21:56.120
Yabuki Joe."

00:21:58.080 --> 00:21:59.130
Thank God!

00:21:59.130 --> 00:22:01.340
You guys made up with each other.

00:22:01.340 --> 00:22:02.300
You should thank us.

00:22:02.300 --> 00:22:03.960
It's because we sent that letter.

00:22:03.960 --> 00:22:06.970
Buy us a present as a thank you!

00:22:07.590 --> 00:22:10.930
Gyoza! Old man, we all want some gyoza.

00:22:07.800 --> 00:22:09.970
<i>Hey, are you listening?</i>

00:22:10.930 --> 00:22:12.970
Hey, are you listening?

00:22:12.060 --> 00:22:14.220
<i>Yeah, yeah, I will.</i>

00:22:14.970 --> 00:22:17.560
Hey, are you listening?

00:22:20.230 --> 00:22:21.230
Stop it, everyone.

00:22:21.230 --> 00:22:22.360
Don't look.

00:22:22.360 --> 00:22:24.440
How come we can't see him?

00:22:22.360 --> 00:22:23.650
<i>S-Stop it.</i>

00:22:24.440 --> 00:22:25.240
I said stop it.

00:22:25.240 --> 00:22:26.320
Hey, hey.

00:22:26.320 --> 00:22:28.660
Yo, Tarou-chan.

00:22:30.620 --> 00:22:31.450
Shut up.

00:22:31.450 --> 00:22:34.700
You guys don't understand how he feels.

00:22:34.700 --> 00:22:39.460
He wants to get a feel for Joe's letter by himself.

00:22:41.040 --> 00:22:42.420
Get a feel for?

00:22:42.420 --> 00:22:44.460
Adults sure are complicated.

00:22:45.170 --> 00:22:46.670
This is amazing!

00:22:47.630 --> 00:22:52.430
It's the first time Joe has spoken seriously about boxing.

00:22:52.430 --> 00:22:53.760
This is great.

00:22:55.220 --> 00:22:56.930
I'm waiting for you, Joe.

00:22:56.930 --> 00:22:59.770
It won't just be a mail order course from now on.

00:22:59.770 --> 00:23:03.230
I'm coming to see you in person immediately.

00:23:12.530 --> 00:23:13.950
All right, everyone,

00:23:13.950 --> 00:23:17.450
let's use his feelings to get him to buy us something!

00:23:18.000 --> 00:23:19.370
I want ramen!

00:23:19.370 --> 00:23:20.960
I want gyoza!

00:24:38.990 --> 00:24:43.000
Joe is now preparing to beat Rikiishi, following his return to prison.

00:24:43.920 --> 00:24:48.000
Joe's only objective now is to train for boxing alone.

00:24:48.000 --> 00:24:53.340
I have just arrived at the island with Joe's little gang.

00:24:53.340 --> 00:24:54.180
Now,

00:24:54.180 --> 00:24:58.350
as he makes a touching reunion, where is Joe's tomorrow!?
